  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIt doesn't seem to be specified what's supposed to happen when a <style> or <link rel=stylesheet> is moved between the document and a shadow root (or between two shadow roots) with moveBefore().\n\n\"Update a style block\" and the link stylesheet processing steps only run on connect, disconnect or other changes a move doesn't trigger, and neither element has moving steps. The sheet is only associated with a document or shadow root when CSSOM first adds it, so read literally it would keep applying to the old tree after the move.\n\nChrome and Firefox both move the sheet to the new tree, and this is what I plan to make WebKit do. Moving steps that move the existing sheet to the new root seem the most natural, but I could be missing something, or this might belong in CSSOM. Moving within the same root seems fine, since order follows tree order.",
